CLOSURE_CHECKS_CLASSIFIER_AUDIT: {
  "schema_version": 1,
  "migration_run_id": "274893c2-7895-4fb2-8644-16e05d91c71c",
  "snapshot_timestamp": "2026-05-21T18:15:12Z",
  "ticket_id": "0e62-ff06",
  "items": [
    {
      "original_text": "On entry to debug-everything, a sub-agent reads debug.gha_workflows from dso-config.conf (comma-separated workflow file names, e.g. ci.yml,deploy.yml). For each listed workflow, it: (a) performs a pre-flight probe (bounded per_page=1 list call); if probe returns tool-not-found, emits \"GHA scan unavailable: workflow run tools not registered\" and exits; (b) fetches the first page of completed (non-pending, non-in-progress, non-queued, non-action_required, non-waiting) runs \u2014 if none found, logs \"GHA scan: no completed run found for <workflow>\" and skips; (c) checks whether an open bug ticket carries the tag gha:<workflow-file-name> \u2014 if yes, skips; otherwise creates a bug ticket with that tag and the workflow file name in the title. If debug.gha_workflows is absent or empty, logs \"GHA scan skipped: no workflows configured\" and continues.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior and workflow process that persists once implemented, despite being phrased with procedural detail"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Between each fix batch in Bug-Fix Mode (regardless of debug.max_fix_validate_cycles setting), debug-everything re-runs the same scan and refreshes the open bug ticket list, creating tickets for newly-detected failures without matching tickets.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes an ongoing system behavior of debug-everything that persists after implementation, not a one-time completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "The GHA scanning sub-agent returns only a compact summary to the orchestrator (workflows checked, new tickets created, failures already tracked); full MCP API response bodies do not appear in the orchestrator context. After each scan dispatch, the orchestrator writes the compact summary as a comment on the active epic ticket.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system behavior where the GHA sub-agent filters and summarizes responses, persisting as an ongoing operational pattern"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "When GitHub MCP workflow run tools are unavailable or return an error, the scan logs a distinguishable signal \u2014 \"GHA scan unavailable: [reason]\" vs \"GHA scan complete: no failures\" \u2014 and debug-everything continues normally.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior where logging and error handling work a specific way during normal operation, not a one-time migration or completion task"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "A config key debug.gha_scan_enabled (default true) allows disabling the scan entirely without affecting other debug-everything behavior.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes a durable system capability (ability to disable a specific scan via config) that persists after implementation"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    },
    {
      "original_text": "Running debug-everything with debug.gha_workflows configured and at least one failing workflow produces: (a) a new bug ticket tagged gha:<workflow-file-name> with the workflow file name in the title, and (b) a GHA scan summary line (with workflows_checked >= 1 and tickets_created >= 1) recorded as a comment on the active epic ticket, including the new ticket ID, summary line verbatim, and the workflow file name.",
      "original_section": "SC",
      "classification": {
        "label": "end-state",
        "ranking": 4,
        "rationale": "describes durable system behavior and output that should occur whenever debug-everything runs with specified conditions, phrased as ongoing expected outcomes"
      },
      "user_decision": "auto",
      "post_migration_section": "SC"
    }
  ]
}
